cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "lean-nock: Jet correctness for Nock, in Lean 4"
abstract: >-
  A Lean 4 mechanization of jet correctness for the Nock 4K combinator
  calculus; the companion artifact to "Jet-Accelerated Code and the
  Co-Design Problem" (N. E. Davis, Urbit Systems Technical Journal). It
  states the three-valued jet contract, proves the two-valued contract
  unsound under virtualization, and develops co-derivation of a Nock
  formula and its native jet from a common concatenative source. Axiom
  footprint {propext, Quot.sound}, build-gated; no Mathlib dependency.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Davis
    given-names: N. E.
    affiliation: ZeroAttest
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/sigilante/lean-nock"
keywords:
  - Nock
  - Urbit
  - jets
  - Lean 4
  - formal verification
  - co-derivation
  - combinator calculus
